            <ArticleTitle>Caesarean delivery during maternal cardiopulmonary resuscitation for status asthmaticus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>296-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient who sustained a recurrent cardiopulmonary resuscitation due to status asthmaticus during one pregnancy followed by a birth of an apparently normal infant is described. Promptly performed caesarean delivery might have saved the mother and her infant. Cardiopulmonary resuscitation is less effective in a near term pregnant woman.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
